description:
A version resource stores the file version `major.minor.build.revision` as two 32-bit numbers. Write

```cpp
struct FileVersion { uint32_t ms{ 0 }; uint32_t ls{ 0 }; };

bool parseFileVersion(const std::string& text, FileVersion& out);
std::string formatFileVersion(const FileVersion& v);
bool isNewer(const FileVersion& candidate, const FileVersion& installed);
```

- `parseFileVersion` reads 1 to 4 parts separated by dots (missing parts are 0: `"2.4"` is `2.4.0.0`). Each part is a whole number from 0 to 65535. Then `ms = major << 16 | minor` and `ls = build << 16 | revision`. Anything else returns `false`.
- `formatFileVersion` gives back all four parts: `"2.4.1.0"`.
- `isNewer` is how an installer decides to replace a file: compare `ms` first, then `ls`.

starter.solution.cpp:
#include <cstdint>
#include <string>

struct FileVersion { uint32_t ms{ 0 }; uint32_t ls{ 0 }; };

bool parseFileVersion(const std::string& text, FileVersion& out) { return false; }
std::string formatFileVersion(const FileVersion& v) { return ""; }
